{
  "case": "render.layout.io-wider-labels",
  "clause": "DESIGN R3.3 \u00a79.4 Region geometry, including Process IO",
  "witness": "labels wider than their IO object widen the footprint; DI label sizes kept, missing label measured; object centres on one row line",
  "derivation": "IO notion label read /name. In_A label 80x14 DI units (80000 x 14000) wider than the 36000 object: footprint 80000, left max(40000, 150000-40000) = 110000, object centred at x 132000, label at 110000. In_B has no BPMNLabel: 'Beta' measured 4 x 600 = 2400 wide, 1000 high; footprint 36000, left 332000, label x 332000+16800. Out_C label 60x14: footprint 60000, desired 320000 collides with 368000+20000 -> 388000, object at 400000. RH = max(80000, 64000+20000) = 84000; A = 25000, B = 25000+14000 = 39000, cy = max(25000, (84000+25000-39000)/2) = 35000: the three object centres share y 35000 (objects at y 10000, labels directly below at y 60000), fixing the per-stack centring of the first seal (centres 43000/49500/43000). Row rule (spec \u00a74.3): items in \u00a77.2 placement order; footprint max(object, label) width; left = anchor centre - footprint/2 when the anchor is shown, else contentLeft or previous right + gap; clamp to contentLeft; collision shifts right; one row at the top of the support body [Ly, Ly+RH], RH = max(minHeight, max(object+label) + 2 padding) (harmonization K2); every object centre lies on one line cy = Ly + max(A, (RH + A - B)/2), A = max h/2, B = max(h/2 + label height), so the union of the stacks is centred in the row (DESIGN \u00a79.4 'align centers on one IO row'); exact rationals, one roundEven per output coordinate. The profile is re-pinned to the lot-4 extension packages neutral-render-descriptors/1 and neutral-render-base/1 (tests/profile_render/expected/artifacts/), which admit every native type of the tree.",
